{"session_id":"019e6a97-9eb6-7e12-a486-d5b37d58ef77","turn_id":"019e6a97-a6f6-7340-a3be-a2beef55230b","transcript_path":null,"cwd":"/Users/sungmin/Dev/claude-plugins/deep-docs","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","model":"gpt-5.5","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"nl -ba README.md | sed -n '70,115p' && nl -ba CLAUDE.md | sed -n '95,155p'"},"tool_response":"    70\t| Stale examples | CLI commands or env variables that don't match `package.json` scripts or `.env.example` | Conditional auto-fix when an exact replacement is known; code examples are audit-only |\n    71\t| Duplicated instructions | Identical blocks (3+ lines, 100% match) repeated across docs | Remove duplicates; near-duplicates are audit-only |\n    72\t\n    73\t### Audit-only (reported, never auto-fixed)\n    74\t\n    75\t| Rule | Description | Why not auto-fixed |\n    76\t|---|---|---|\n    77\t| Size/organization | `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` >100, `README.md` >300, other `docs/` >200 lines | Splitting needs structural judgment |\n    78\t| Rule–code contradiction | Doc says \"use snake_case\" but most code uses camelCase | Architecture judgment; high false-positive risk |\n    79\t| Coverage gaps | Major modules not mentioned anywhere in docs | \"Major\" is subjective |\n    80\t| Map vs manual ratio | Ratio of direct instructions to external pointers | Optimal ratio varies per project |\n    81\t\n    82\t### Authoring (created/restructured by `garden`)\n    83\t\n    84\t| Rule | Description | How it is handled |\n    85\t|---|---|---|\n    86\t| Missing doc | A recommended `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` (build manifest + source dirs) or `ARCHITECTURE.md` (~10k+ LOC) does not exist | `garden` drafts it from a code analysis and writes it after approval |\n    87\t| Thin doc | An existing doc falls clearly short of its official skeleton | `garden` restructures it, preserving your unique content by default |\n    88\t\n    89\tAuthoring uses built-in rules from `skills/deep-docs-workflow/references/authoring-rules/` (CLAUDE.md follows Anthropic's memory guide, AGENTS.md the OpenAI Codex/agents.md standard, ARCHITECTURE.md the matklad standard). Length targets are soft for `CLAUDE.md`/`ARCHITECTURE.md` line counts (an over-long draft is reported as a non-blocking size warning, matching the line-based `audit`), while `AGENTS.md` enforces a hard 32&nbsp;KiB byte ceiling (Codex truncates beyond it) — note this byte/line asymmetry: authoring considers the Codex byte budget, `audit` stays line-based.\n    90\t\n    91\t## Garden workflow\n    92\t\n    93\tWhen you run `/deep-docs garden`, the agent:\n    94\t\n    95\t1. **Reuses** `.deep-docs/last-scan.json` if it is fresh (under 10 minutes old, matching HEAD and worktree); otherwise re-runs the scan first.\n    96\t2. **Filters to auto-fixable issues** only — size warnings stay in the audit-only summary.\n    97\t3. **For each issue**, shows a diff and asks for confirmation before applying the edit.\n    98\t4. **Authoring sub-flow** — for each `gaps[]` entry, `garden` spawns the read-only `doc-author` agent, receives a structured draft, captures a TOCTOU baseline (so a file changed since the scan is never silently overwritten), asks per-removal whether to apply / revise / keep, re-inserts any unapproved removals, and only then writes the file itself. `doc-author` never writes — it has no `Write` or `Bash` tool.\n    99\t5. **Summarizes** fixes applied, documents authored, skipped, and audit-only items noted for reference.\n   100\t\n   101\tAudit-only items are always shown at the end as informational notes, never modified automatically.\n   102\t\n   103\t> **Empty/new-repo note:** authoring gaps surface through `/deep-docs scan|garden` directly. Until deep-dashboard consumes `gaps[]`, the authoring backlog for an empty or brand-new repository (no existing documents) is **not visible on the dashboard** — the document-health metrics there only count issues found in existing documents.\n   104\t\n   105\t## Audit metrics\n   106\t\n   107\t`/deep-docs audit` scores each document across four measurable dimensions:\n   108\t\n   109\t| Metric | How it is measured | Scoring |\n   110\t|---|---|---|\n   111\t| Size | Line count vs recommended limit | `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`: ≤100 = 10, 100–200 = 7, >200 = 4 |\n   112\t| Freshness | Are any referenced paths newer than the doc? | All fresh = 10, some stale = 7, mostly stale = 4 |\n   113\t| Reference accuracy | Valid references / total references | 100% = 10, 90–99% = 8, 70–89% = 5, <70% = 2 |\n   114\t| Duplication | Duplicate blocks shared with other docs | 0 = 10, 1–2 = 7, ≥3 = 4 |\n   115\t\n    95\t---\n    96\t\n    97\t## Key Concepts\n    98\t\n    99\t### `last-scan.json` envelope + payload schema\n   100\t\n   101\t```\n   102\tRoot:\n   103\t  $schema: <URL of artifact-envelope.schema.json>\n   104\t  schema_version: \"1.0\"                # envelope wrapper version (string, not numeric)\n   105\t  envelope: { ... }\n   106\t  payload: { ... }\n   107\t\n   108\tenvelope.producer:          \"deep-docs\"\n   109\tenvelope.producer_version:  literal sync with plugin.json.version (enforced)\n   110\tenvelope.artifact_kind:     \"last-scan\"\n   111\tenvelope.schema:            { name: \"last-scan\", version: \"1.1\" }   # payload schema; top-level schema_version stays \"1.0\"\n   112\tenvelope.run_id:            ULID (26-char Crockford Base32, MSB-first, no I/L/O/U)\n   113\tenvelope.generated_at:      RFC 3339 UTC second-precision\n   114\tenvelope.git:               { head: 7–40 hex (or \"0000000\" non-git), branch, dirty: bool|\"unknown\" }\n   115\tenvelope.provenance:        { source_artifacts: [{ path }, ...], tool_versions: { node, python, ... } }\n   116\t\n   117\tpayload.provenance.is_git:              bool\n   118\tpayload.provenance.worktree_hash:       sha1 40-hex (tracked + untracked files NUL-safe,\n   119\t                                        per-file `git hash-object`) or \"no-git\"\n   120\tpayload.provenance.path_check_enabled:  optional — emitted ONLY when cli-whitelist PATH-check is ON\n   121\t\n   122\tpayload.documents[]:           # existing documents only\n   123\t  - path\n   124\t  - issues[]:\n   125\t      - type:               dead-reference | moved-path | stale-example | duplicate-block | size-warning\n   126\t      - category:           \"auto-fix\" | \"audit-only\"\n   127\t      - severity\n   128\t      - line\n   129\t      - current_value\n   130\t      - suggested_value     # null when category === \"audit-only\"\n   131\t      - evidence\n   132\t  - metrics:\n   133\t      - size_lines\n   134\t      - freshness_score:    null | 10 | 7 | 4\n   135\t      - reference_accuracy: 0.0 – 1.0\n   136\t      - duplication_count\n   137\t\n   138\tpayload.gaps[]:                # optional — authoring (missing/thin recommended docs). NOT a reuse-guard input.\n   139\t  - type:                 missing-doc | thin-doc\n   140\t  - category:             \"authoring\"\n   141\t  - severity\n   142\t  - target_path:          root-only exact (CLAUDE.md | AGENTS.md | ARCHITECTURE.md); no nested/traversal\n   143\t  - exists:               false (missing-doc) | true (thin-doc)\n   144\t  - evidence\n   145\t  - authoring_spec:       { doc_kind: claude-md|agents-md|architecture-md, mode: create|restructure, rationale }\n   146\t                          # draft body NOT here — garden's doc-author generates it\n   147\t\n   148\tpayload.summary:  { total_issues, auto_fixable, authoring, audit_only }\n   149\t                  # total_issues/auto_fixable/audit_only = documents[].issues[] ONLY (gaps excluded — dashboard metric preserved, D12)\n   150\t                  # authoring = gaps[] length\n   151\t```\n   152\t\n   153\t### Reuse guard (5-element)\n   154\t\n   155\tA `last-scan.json` is reusable if **all five** match:\n","tool_use_id":"call_nXb3iYcRd0k2jOz0HPicpH3F"}